# Adobe Artifactory (npm) — supplemental notes
#
# Root `.npmrc` commits `@pim:registry` (no token) so scoped packages resolve to
# the same registry used for publish, without repeating `publishConfig` per package.
#
# Writable internal npm (typical Adobe pattern): **npm-adobe-release** on Corp
# Artifactory — requires VPN / corporate network for many environments:
#   https://artifactory.corp.adobe.com/artifactory/api/npm/npm-adobe-release/
#
# UW2 cloud mirror (`.../api/npm/npmjs/`) is often read/cached only; if you see
# "no deploy permissions" there, publish to **npm-adobe-release** (or the repo
# your admin names) instead. Confirm the exact URL in Artifactory "Set me up"
# for that repository.
#
# Unscoped `ado-pim` uses `publishConfig.registry` in packages/cli/package.json.
#
# Auth — user ~/.npmrc or CI (never commit tokens). Example for Corp host:
# //artifactory.corp.adobe.com/artifactory/api/npm/npm-adobe-release/:_authToken=${NPM_TOKEN}
# always-auth=true
#
# Other approved read mirrors (if your doc points installs here instead):
# https://artifactory-uw2.adobeitc.com/artifactory/api/npm/npmjs/
# https://artifactory.corp.adobe.com/artifactory/api/npm/npmjs/
# https://artifactory-no1.corp.adobe.com/artifactory/api/npm/npmjs/
